<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) & Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) ocular dominance column development & plasticity (Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC))",
        "Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) & Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) ocular dominance column development & plasticity faithfully reproduces Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/miller-ocular-dominance-stripes-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/miller-ocular-dominance-stripes-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/miller-ocular-dominance-stripes-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-ocular-dominance-stripes-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py> ;
    schema:about "Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular NMDA receptor channel kinetics, cytochrome oxidase blob co-alignment with orientation pinwheels in Layers 2/3, or curved calcarine sulcus 3D cortical folding geometry",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D spectral Miller-Keller-Stryker / Swindale solver on a 96x96 periodic tangential V1 Layer IVC sheet (6400x6400 um) across all 5 canonical regimes plus a 6-point intracortical inhibition range sigma_I wavelength sweep (170-290 um, Pearson r = 0.9970)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated CV segmentation of stripe territories (f_L = 0.5000), 2D Hanning FFT spectral peak (16 cycles, 800 um scaled wavelength), and N = 71 Y-branchpoints on `odc_tangential_pattern_specimen.png` plus Layer IVC laminar Nissl optical density profiling (s* = 0.35) on `macaque_striate_cortex_specimen.jpg`",
        "reported_in_source: Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 278:377-409 tangential autoradiographs of Macaca mulatta V1 Layer IVC showing ~400 um single-eye column width (~800 um full wavelength), monocular deprivation shrinkage of deprived-eye stripes into narrow islands, and critical-period reverse suture rescue",
        "reported_in_source: Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) Science 245:605-615 correlation-based Hebbian synaptic competition model showing that subtractive homeostatic normalization conserves S_Sigma = S^L + S^R while S_Delta = S^L - S^R amplifies at the Mexican-hat band-pass peak k_c",
        "reported_in_source: Stryker & Harris (1986) J. Neurosci. 6:2117-2133 showing that bilateral intraocular TTX retinal impulse blockade (C_Delta = 0) completely prevents ocular dominance column segregation",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D tangential Layer IVC cortical sheet x in [0, 6.4 mm]^2 with isotropic Difference-of-Gaussians lateral interaction I(r) and coupled S^L, S^R synaptic densities" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py; output: docs/media/ocular_dominance_stripes_comparison.png; organism: Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 819128bbec5b994d73c8b186f4a86b2d2df6149663f61bdaf866cb36447d290f; artifact_sha256: d9836de9bccac0673460f380c616ad3321ffc7b4d515cc99a0a2314c303799eb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/macaque_striate_cortex_specimen.jpg=fe74eb6f9db7dea1..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/ocular_dominance_stripes_reference.json=7041693bc0b54b31..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/odc_tangential_pattern_specimen.png=fac59bb151b4eb1d..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/paper_citations.bib=29c3ea74bae42954..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/scout_manifest.json=2f54657c6b0c2050...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-ocular-dominance-stripes-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) Science 245:605-615 correlation-based Hebbian synaptic competition model showing that subtractive homeostatic normalization conserves S_Sigma = S^L + S^R while S_Delta = S^L - S^R amplifies at the Mexican-hat band-pass peak k_c | Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 278:377-409 tangential autoradiographs of Macaca mulatta V1 Layer IVC showing ~400 um single-eye column width (~800 um full wavelength), monocular deprivation shrinkage of deprived-eye stripes into narrow islands, and critical-period reverse suture rescue | Stryker & Harris (1986) J. Neurosci. 6:2117-2133 showing that bilateral intraocular TTX retinal impulse blockade (C_Delta = 0) completely prevents ocular dominance column segregation; reconstructed_in_script: 2D spectral Miller-Keller-Stryker / Swindale solver on a 96x96 periodic tangential V1 Layer IVC sheet (6400x6400 um) across all 5 canonical regimes plus a 6-point intracortical inhibition range sigma_I wavelength sweep (170-290 um, Pearson r = 0.9970) | Automated CV segmentation of stripe territories (f_L = 0.5000), 2D Hanning FFT spectral peak (16 cycles, 800 um scaled wavelength), and N = 71 Y-branchpoints on `odc_tangential_pattern_specimen.png` plus Layer IVC laminar Nissl optical density profiling (s* = 0.35) on `macaque_striate_cortex_specimen.jpg`; transfer_boundary: 2D tangential Layer IVC cortical sheet x in [0, 6.4 mm]^2 with isotropic Difference-of-Gaussians lateral interaction I(r) and coupled S^L, S^R synaptic densities; does_not_claim: Subcellular NMDA receptor channel kinetics, cytochrome oxidase blob co-alignment with orientation pinwheels in Layers 2/3, or curved calcarine sulcus 3D cortical folding geometry]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0051>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1977.0050>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.2762813>,
