<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) & Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) ocular dominance column development & plasticity — MorphoEval overall 92.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py` (92.9/100, up from 57.7/100 in Pass 1; +35.2 overall). The remediated script solves the 2D Miller-Keller-Stryker / Swindale integro-differential ocular dominance PDE on a 96x96 periodic V1 Layer IVC tangential sheet (`6400 x 6400 um`) tracking coupled left/right synaptic densities `S^L(x,t), S^R(x,t)` under subtractive normalization (`max |S^L + S^R - S_Sigma| < 1e-15`) across all 5 canonical experimental regimes: Normal Binocular 50/50 zebra stripes (`f_L = 0.5036`, `lambda = 806.19 um` vs `800.26 um` analytical band-pass peak), Hubel-Wiesel Critical-Period Monocular Deprivation shrunken bands/islands (`f_L = 0.2533`, `f_R = 0.7467`), Strabismus decorrelated broadened columns (`lambda = 883.82 um`, `SI = 0.9806`), Stryker-Harris Bilateral TTX Impulse Blockade unsegregated control (`SI = 0.0029 < 0.01`), and Reverse Suture critical-period rescue (`f_L = 0.6844`), paired with a 6-point intracortical inhibition range `sigma_I` sweep (`r = 0.9970`, `RMSE = 13.36 um`), automated CV segmentation of the tangential ODC and *Macaca mulatta* V1 Layer IVC specimens, and 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_087_ocular_dominance_stripes.lean`. Overall 92.8/100 (faithfulness 92.7, reproducibility 93.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/ocular_dominance_stripes_comparison.png: rendered output of 1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1765310 B, 2227×1863 px, artifact_sha256 d9836de9bccac0673460f380c616ad3321ffc7b4d515cc99a0a2314c303799eb (sha256 d9836de9bccac0673460f380c616ad3321ffc7b4d515cc99a0a2314c303799eb), spec_fingerprint 819128bbec5b994d73c8b186f4a86b2d2df6149663f61bdaf866cb36447d290f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 819128bbec5b994d73c8b186f4a86b2d2df6149663f61bdaf866cb36447d290f; artifact_sha256: d9836de9bccac0673460f380c616ad3321ffc7b4d515cc99a0a2314c303799eb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/macaque_striate_cortex_specimen.jpg=fe74eb6f9db7dea1..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/ocular_dominance_stripes_reference.json=7041693bc0b54b31..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/odc_tangential_pattern_specimen.png=fac59bb151b4eb1d..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/paper_citations.bib=29c3ea74bae42954..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/scout_manifest.json=2f54657c6b0c2050...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-ocular-dominance-stripes-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) Science 245:605-615 correlation-based Hebbian synaptic competition model showing that subtractive homeostatic normalization conserves S_Sigma = S^L + S^R while S_Delta = S^L - S^R amplifies at the Mexican-hat band-pass peak k_c | Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 278:377-409 tangential autoradiographs of Macaca mulatta V1 Layer IVC showing ~400 um single-eye column width (~800 um full wavelength), monocular deprivation shrinkage of deprived-eye stripes into narrow islands, and critical-period reverse suture rescue | Stryker & Harris (1986) J. Neurosci. 6:2117-2133 showing that bilateral intraocular TTX retinal impulse blockade (C_Delta = 0) completely prevents ocular dominance column segregation; reconstructed_in_script: 2D spectral Miller-Keller-Stryker / Swindale solver on a 96x96 periodic tangential V1 Layer IVC sheet (6400x6400 um) across all 5 canonical regimes plus a 6-point intracortical inhibition range sigma_I wavelength sweep (170-290 um, Pearson r = 0.9970) | Automated CV segmentation of stripe territories (f_L = 0.5000), 2D Hanning FFT spectral peak (16 cycles, 800 um scaled wavelength), and N = 71 Y-branchpoints on `odc_tangential_pattern_specimen.png` plus Layer IVC laminar Nissl optical density profiling (s* = 0.35) on `macaque_striate_cortex_specimen.jpg`; transfer_boundary: 2D tangential Layer IVC cortical sheet x in [0, 6.4 mm]^2 with isotropic Difference-of-Gaussians lateral interaction I(r) and coupled S^L, S^R synaptic densities; does_not_claim: Subcellular NMDA receptor channel kinetics, cytochrome oxidase blob co-alignment with orientation pinwheels in Layers 2/3, or curved calcarine sulcus 3D cortical folding geometry." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D ocular dominance field S_Delta(x,y) to a complex orientation preference field z(x,y) = r(x,y)*exp(2*i*theta(x,y)) to model orthogonal intersection of iso-orientation contours with ocular dominance borders and cytochrome oxidase blob alignment.",
        "remediation needed: Extend the flat periodic domain to a curved 2D Riemannian manifold matching the anatomical perimeter of the macaque V1 operculum and calcarine sulcus." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.28e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

